The two that carry this lane's claim:
  MV-WIRE-01: one send makes exactly one /api request, and it is /api/chat
  MV-WIRE-02: no poller keeps running after the reply lands

MV-WIRE-01 asserts on the wire, not the source: it records every request the
page makes from the moment the send starts and requires the list to equal
exactly ['/api/chat'] — no /api/realtime*, no /api/chat-with-vic*, no WebSocket,
no page errors — and requires a real reply (>40 chars) to render. The panel is
opened the way tests/monochrome/minivic-launcher.spec.ts opens it (wait for
React hydration on the launcher, scroll past the hero, click through the
element); that is the step the independent reviewer was missing when the panel
would not open for them in headless Chrome and they measured zero /api/*
requests.

MV-WIRE-02 watches a 7-second window after the reply — wider than the removed
poller's 3-second interval — and requires silence.

